Landor is looking for an Executive Assistant to join our Cincinnati studio. Could this be you? &nbsp;

 

We are Landor, part of WPP

World-leading brand experts,&nbsp;
underpinned by the most expansive strategic &amp; creative capabilities in our category.

We make brands more valuable and less vulnerable.

We build brands differently. We work with our clients to define and solve their business problems through the lens of brand. We strategically join the dots between our design, experience, governance and measurement capabilities, and always connect our brand work to business outcomes.&nbsp;

Landor companies also include amp (sonic branding), bdg (workplace &amp; architectural experts), Deep Local (creative technologists) and ManvsMachine (3D motion design).

About WPP

WPP is the trusted growth partner for the world’s leading brands. We unite&nbsp;cutting-edge media intelligence and data solutions, world-class creativity, next-generation production, transformative enterprise solutions and expert strategic counsel&nbsp;in a single company -&nbsp;powered by exceptional talent and our agentic marketing platform, WPP Open,&nbsp;to help our clients navigate change, capture opportunity and deliver transformational growth. For more information, visit&nbsp; WPP.com .

We are looking for a highly organized, energetic superstar to join our team as an Administrative Assistant. The ideal candidate is a trusted professional and will act as an extension of the leadership team in terms of voice,&nbsp;judgment&nbsp;and decision making. You are comfortable managing&nbsp;highly sensitive&nbsp;information and&nbsp;maintain&nbsp;incredibly&nbsp;high standards&nbsp;of confidentiality. &nbsp;

You will be experienced in handling a wide range of administrative and executive support related tasks and will be able to work independently. This person thrives at being mindful of details in a fast-paced environment with a diverse group of people, at all levels. This position will play an integral role in the daily flow,&nbsp;success&nbsp;and operations of Landor. &nbsp;

If you consider yourself a hungry, proactive,&nbsp;thoughtful&nbsp;and kind professional, who is looking to learn from top tier talent in a fast-paced agency setting, this could be the role for you. &nbsp;

• Build a partnership with the executives and work together positively and effectively. &nbsp;

• Work closely and effectively with the executives to keep them well informed of upcoming commitments and responsibilities, following up appropriately. Acts as a "barometer," having a sense for the issues taking place in the environment and keeping the Executives updated. &nbsp;

• Act as a brand ambassador for not only the executives but Landor as a whole.&nbsp;Being the first point of contact for many clients and&nbsp;stakeholders&nbsp;the ideal candidate will always present themselves as an extension of the executives. &nbsp;

• Act as the executives’ right hand,&nbsp;anticipating&nbsp;needs for maximum efficiency and impact with all communications, tasks, meetings &amp; projects. &nbsp;

• Effectively and respectfully communicate with internal and external stakeholders in a variety of different formats. &nbsp;

• Tackle&nbsp;any and all&nbsp;tasks to ensure the executives can maximize their time to focus on strategic areas relating to the ongoing development of the business. &nbsp;

• Adapt to changing demands and responsibilities quickly. A true problem solver, someone who can pivot without missing a step. &nbsp;

• Manage full calendar and scheduling commitments. &nbsp;

• Organize intricate global travel and&nbsp;anticipate&nbsp;last minute changes. &nbsp;

• Coordinate internal/external meetings,&nbsp;logistics&nbsp;and communications. &nbsp;

• Act as the host of the studio, caring for guests and team members alike, and&nbsp;maintaining&nbsp;an environment that is&nbsp;conducive to collaboration and&nbsp;a&nbsp;positive, enjoyable&nbsp;culture &nbsp;

  &nbsp;

About you &nbsp;

With millions of diners, 70,000+ restaurant partners and 25+ years of experience, OpenTable, part of Booking Holdings, Inc. (NASDAQ: BKNG), is an industry leader with a passion for helping restaurants thrive. Our world-class technology empowers restaurants to focus on what matters most - their team, their guests, and their bottom line - while enabling diners to discover and book the perfect restaurant for every occasion.&nbsp;

Every employee at OpenTable has a tangible impact on what we do and how we do it. You’ll also be part of a global team and its portfolio of metasearch brands. Hospitality is all about taking care of others, and it defines our culture.

&nbsp;

About the Job

The EU engineering team in London is looking to hire an Android Engineer to join our team on a 12 month fixed term contract basis. In this role, you will work to strengthen the infrastructure behind our app, used by millions of diners worldwide. You will play a crucial role in improving the foundations of a large Kotlin codebase while shaping the technical roadmap for new data integrations and architecture. By collaborating across teams, you will help build and maintain the Android capabilities that support our marketing technology initiatives, including attribution and deep linking. Ultimately, your work will empower restaurants to thrive by creating reliable, high-performance experiences that encourage diners to return time and again.

Note: This is a 12 month fixed term contract.&nbsp;

Responsibilities

• Shape the technical roadmap of new data integrations, application architecture, and scalability efforts.

• Enhance the core Android app’s architecture to ensure the codebase remains maintainable, scalable, and modern.</li&

